# Select an environment from http-client.env.json in Rider's "Run with" menu.
# A value named apiToken in http-client.private.env.json overrides this OS variable.
@apiToken = {{$env.OFFICEDAYS_API_TOKEN}}

# Status uses the requirement effective in the selected month.
# DaysPerWeek mode converts to an equivalent percentage (days * 20).
# Required office days round up: ceil(eligible working days * percentage / 100).
# Responses retain the existing totals and add a summary object:
# today (user timezone), totalDays, workingDays, bankHolidayWorkingDays,
# vacationWorkingDays, requirementMode, requirementValue,
# requiredOfficeDaysWithoutAbsences, plannedDays, remainingEligibleDays,
# outstandingOfficeDays, bankHolidays [{date, name}], vacationDates [date].
# Holiday/vacation lists include every matching date in the requested month,
# including weekends. Weekday deductions count overlaps once: bank holidays first,
# then vacation weekdays that are not bank holidays.
# plannedDays counts all eligible plans in the month; upcomingPlannedDays excludes
# past and attended dates. Plans never count as attendance.
# remainingEligibleDays includes today when eligible and not already attended.
# outstandingOfficeDays = max(0, remainingOfficeDays - remainingEligibleDays).
### Current user's current-month status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/status
Authorization: Bearer {{apiToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Selected-month status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/status?year=2026&month=9
Authorization: Bearer {{apiToken}}
Accept: application/json
